# Static hosts that support `_headers` (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages) will send
# these headers for every response. GitHub Pages ignores the file, so the app
# keeps its CSP meta tag as the baseline; frame-ancestors is only enforced when
# delivered as a real header (browsers ignore it inside <meta>).

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
